{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nconst int mod = 1000000007;\nint n, S, cnt[250], id[250];\nint f[10][250];\nvector<int> vec[10];\nmap<pair<long long, int>, int> mp;\n\nint pow_mod(int x, int y) {\n    int res = 1;\n    while (y) {\n        if (y & 1) res = (long long)res * x % mod;\n        x = (long long)x * x % mod;\n        y >>= 1;\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nint DP(int x, long long sta) {\n    if (!sta) return 0;\n    if (x == n) return 1;\n    long long key = (long long)x << 60 | sta; // combine into single key\n    if (mp.find({key, 0}) != mp.end()) return mp[{key, 0}];\n    ++S;\n    int ans = 0;\n    for (int j = 1; j < (1 << n); ++j) {\n        long long nxt = 0;\n        for (int k = 0; k < (int)vec[x].size(); ++k) {\n            if (!(sta & (1LL << k))) continue;\n            int las = vec[x][k];\n            for (int l = 0; l < n; ++l) {\n                if ((j & (1 << l)) && !(las & (1 << l)))\n                    nxt |= 1LL << id[las | (1 << l)];\n            }\n        }\n        ans = (ans + (long long)f[x][j] * DP(x + 1, nxt)) % mod;\n    }\n    mp[{key, 0}] = ans;\n    return ans;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    scanf(\"%d\", &n);\n    int inv100 = pow_mod(100, mod - 2);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        f[i][0] = 1;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            int P;\n            scanf(\"%d\", &P);\n            int p1 = (long long)P * inv100 % mod;\n            int p0 = (mod + 1 - p1) % mod;\n            for (int k = 0; k < (1 << j); ++k) {\n                f[i][k | (1 << j)] = (long long)f[i][k] * p1 % mod;\n                f[i][k] = (long long)f[i][k] * p0 % mod;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    for (int i = 0; i < (1 << n); ++i)\n        cnt[i] = cnt[i / 2] + (i & 1);\n    for (int i = 0; i < (1 << n); ++i) {\n        vec[cnt[i]].push_back(i);\n        id[i] = (int)vec[cnt[i]].size() - 1;\n    }\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", DP(0, 1));\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final int MOD = 1000000007;\n    static int n;\n    static int[] cnt = new int[250];\n    static int[] id = new int[250];\n    static int[][] f = new int[10][250];\n    static ArrayList<Integer>[] vec = new ArrayList[10];\n    static HashMap<Long, Integer> mp = new HashMap<>();\n\n    static int pow_mod(int x, int y) {\n        int res = 1;\n        while (y > 0) {\n            if ((y & 1) == 1) res = (int)((long)res * x % MOD);\n            x = (int)((long)x * x % MOD);\n            y >>= 1;\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n\n    static int DP(int x, long sta) {\n        if (sta == 0) return 0;\n        if (x == n) return 1;\n        long key = ((long)x << 60) | sta;\n        if (mp.containsKey(key)) return mp.get(key);\n        int ans = 0;\n        for (int j = 1; j < (1 << n); ++j) {\n            long nxt = 0;\n            for (int k = 0; k < vec[x].size(); ++k) {\n                if ((sta & (1L << k)) == 0) continue;\n         